# Object.defineProperties(target, map): the questions that a descriptor answers (get, set, value, writable, enumerable, configurable) were asked of the map itself, one level too high: an entry NAMED writable answered, and
# the whole map was let go. The library's map of Writable's accessors has such an entry. A map each of whose entries lays an accessor as written is not inspected: all that the built-in takes out of it is laid by name.
